  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="69.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 69.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ gif hwa æfter ðam wite crafige, beo he his weres scyldig wið þone cingc.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ gif hwa æfter wite crafige, be his weres scyldig wið þonne cyningc.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et si quis forisfacturam inde crauabit, wérę suę reus sit erga regem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-b">And gyf hwá æfter ðam wite crauian [wille], beo he his weres scyldig wið ðone cyningc.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gif hwa æfter ðam wite crafige, beo he his weres scyldig wið þone cingc.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And if anyone [of my reeves] shall demand a fine [in such a case], he shall forfeit his wergeld to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And if any of my reeves solicits a bribe, his wergild shall be forfeit to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And if anyone after this demands a fine, he is to forfeit his wergild to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn nach diesem [Zeitpunkt] einer [der Vögte für Gastung] Strafgeld einfordert, sei er sein Wergeld schuldig gegenüber dem König.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if after this [time] anyone [of the reeves] demands a fine [for hospitality], let him be liable for his wergild to the king.</ab>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ðam: omitted A</note>
      </div>
    </body>
